# govulncheck waivers for the bashy seaweedfs verified build.
#
# One OSV id per line (GO-YYYY-NNNN), followed by a justification on the same
# line or in the comment above it. The audit job fails on any REACHABLE
# vulnerability — one whose first trace frame names a called function — that is
# not listed here. An empty list (this file) means nothing is waived.
#
# A waiver is a review decision, not a convenience: record who accepted it,
# why the reachable path cannot be exploited in bashy's configuration, and what
# would retire it (an upstream pin bump, almost always).
#
# NOTHING IS WAIVED HERE, and the reachable findings 4.48 does have are fixed
# rather than waived: see GO_TOOLCHAIN_SECURITY_OVERRIDE (12 stdlib findings)
# and GO_SECURITY_OVERRIDES (5 golang.org/x/net findings) in ../tool.env. The
# three findings govulncheck still reports at this pin are MODULE-level only —
# GO-2022-0635 and GO-2022-0646 (github.com/aws/aws-sdk-go) and GO-2026-5932
# (golang.org/x/crypto) have no called-function trace frame — so they are
# informational and the gate does not consider them.
